-- Tests for ss 6 to 12, the Fourth Schedule and the Fifth Schedule.  Expectations are
-- read off the text: $30,000 in s 6(6); 2 years in s 6(9); 5 and 10 years in s 9(7) and
-- (10); 14 days in s 9(4)(d); 6 months in s 9(12); 2 years, 1 year in s 12; 15% in the
-- Fifth Schedule.

§ `Tests -- Part 2, ss 6 to 12`

§§ `6. Consumer's right to sue for unfair practice`

`no valuation facts` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- Consumer Action Facts: entered a transaction involving an unfair practice, commenced
-- against the supplier, claim for money, amount of claim, set-off admitted, balance
-- after set-off, subject matter is residential property, value if not residential,
-- valuation facts, abandoned the excess, limit prescribed in place of $30,000.

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a money claim of` amount MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, amount, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, `no valuation facts`, FALSE, NOTHING

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a money claim abandoned down from` amount MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, amount, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, `no valuation facts`, TRUE, NOTHING

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      balance IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a money claim of` amount `reduced by an admitted set-off to` balance MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, amount, TRUE, balance, FALSE, 0, `no valuation facts`, FALSE, NOTHING

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a money claim of` amount `where the Minister has prescribed` limit MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, amount, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, `no valuation facts`, FALSE, JUST limit

GIVEN value IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a claim with no money sought over subject matter worth` value MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, value, `no valuation facts`, FALSE, NOTHING

GIVEN value IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a claim with no money sought, the excess abandoned, over subject matter worth` value MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, value, `no valuation facts`, TRUE, NOTHING

GIVEN v IS A `Residential Valuation Facts`
GIVETH A `Consumer Action Facts`
`a claim with no money sought over a dwelling valued by` v MEANS
    `Consumer Action Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, TRUE, 0, v, FALSE, NOTHING

#ASSERT `the prescribed limit` (`a money claim of` 1_000) EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT `the prescribed limit` (`a money claim of` 1_000 `where the Minister has prescribed` 50_000) EQUALS 50_000

-- the boundary in s 6(2)(a) and (6)
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 30_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 30_001)
-- s 6(5): abandoning the excess brings the claim within the limit, and caps recovery
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim abandoned down from` 45_000)
#ASSERT `the most that the consumer may recover in the action` (`a money claim abandoned down from` 45_000) EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT `the most that the consumer may recover in the action` (`a money claim of` 12_000) EQUALS 12_000
-- s 6(3): a balance within the limit after an admitted set-off is not taken to exceed it
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 45_000 `reduced by an admitted set-off to` 30_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 45_000 `reduced by an admitted set-off to` 30_001)
-- s 6(6): a limit the Minister has prescribed replaces $30,000
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 40_000 `where the Minister has prescribed` 50_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a money claim of` 60_000 `where the Minister has prescribed` 50_000)
-- s 6(2)(b): no claim for money, subject matter over the limit
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over subject matter worth` 30_000)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over subject matter worth` 30_001)
-- s 6(5) speaks of "the amount of a claim"; abandonment does not rescue a claim with no amount
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought, the excess abandoned, over subject matter worth` 40_000)
-- s 6(1): the consumer must have entered a consumer transaction involving an unfair practice
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`Consumer Action Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 100, FALSE, 0, FALSE, 0, `no valuation facts`, FALSE, NOTHING)

-- s 6(4): the value of a dwelling
--                                        annual value,    annual rent,  monthly rent,  last transacted price
`annual value 25000 and rent 24000 a year` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF JUST 25_000, JUST 24_000, NOTHING, NOTHING
`annual value 35000 and rent 30000 a year` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF JUST 35_000, JUST 30_000, NOTHING, NOTHING
`annual value 35000 and rent 40000 a year` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF JUST 35_000, JUST 40_000, NOTHING, NOTHING
`annual value 35000 and rent 2000 a month` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF JUST 35_000, NOTHING, JUST 2_000, NOTHING
`annual value 20000 only` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF JUST 20_000, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING
`only a last price of 400000` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST 400_000
`only a last price of 250000` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST 250_000
`nothing ascertainable` MEANS `Residential Valuation Facts` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `annual value 25000 and rent 24000 a year` EQUALS 24_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `annual value 35000 and rent 30000 a year` EQUALS 30_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `annual value 35000 and rent 40000 a year` EQUALS 35_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `annual value 35000 and rent 2000 a month` EQUALS 24_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `annual value 20000 only` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `only a last price of 400000` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `the value of residential property` `only a last price of 250000` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the value of residential property` `nothing ascertainable`

#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over a dwelling valued by` `annual value 35000 and rent 30000 a year`)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over a dwelling valued by` `annual value 35000 and rent 40000 a year`)
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over a dwelling valued by` `only a last price of 400000`)
#ASSERT `the consumer may commence an action under section 6(1)` (`a claim with no money sought over a dwelling valued by` `only a last price of 250000`)

-- s 6(7), (8), (9): stay and discontinuance
-- Stay Facts: a party applies, s 9 application made against the same supplier, proceedings relate
-- to it, court satisfied it will be material, date of stay order, date of last further step, date considered.
`a stay is sought and the s 9 application is material` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, NOTHING, YMD 2026 1 15
`a stay is sought but the s 9 outcome is not material` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2024 1 15, NOTHING, YMD 2026 1 15
`a stay is sought but no s 9 application has been made` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, NOTHING, YMD 2026 1 15
`stayed on 15 Jan 2024, nothing since, considered exactly 2 years on` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, NOTHING, YMD 2026 1 15
`stayed on 15 Jan 2024, nothing since, considered a day short of 2 years` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, NOTHING, YMD 2026 1 14
`stayed on 15 Jan 2024, a step on 1 Jun 2024, considered 15 Jan 2026` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, JUST (YMD 2024 6 1), YMD 2026 1 15
`stayed on 15 Jan 2024, a step on 1 Jun 2024, considered 1 Jun 2026` MEANS `Stay Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2024 1 15, JUST (YMD 2024 6 1), YMD 2026 6 1

#ASSERT `the court may stay the proceedings` `a stay is sought and the s 9 application is material`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may stay the proceedings` `a stay is sought but the s 9 outcome is not material`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may stay the proceedings` `a stay is sought but no s 9 application has been made`
#ASSERT `a party may apply to stay the proceedings` `a stay is sought but the s 9 outcome is not material`
#ASSERT NOT `a party may apply to stay the proceedings` `a stay is sought but no s 9 application has been made`
#ASSERT `the court may of its own motion discontinue the stayed proceedings` `stayed on 15 Jan 2024, nothing since, considered exactly 2 years on`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may of its own motion discontinue the stayed proceedings` `stayed on 15 Jan 2024, nothing since, considered a day short of 2 years`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may of its own motion discontinue the stayed proceedings` `stayed on 15 Jan 2024, a step on 1 Jun 2024, considered 15 Jan 2026`
#ASSERT `the court may of its own motion discontinue the stayed proceedings` `stayed on 15 Jan 2024, a step on 1 Jun 2024, considered 1 Jun 2026`

§§ `7. Jurisdiction and powers of courts`

-- Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts: kind of action, relates to the unfair practice or undertaking, contract
-- is one in para 1(a) or (c) of the SCT Act schedule, relates to sale of immovable property, time share.
`a s 6(1) action on a relevant contract` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under section 6(1)`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a s 6(1) action on a contract for the sale of immovable property` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under section 6(1)`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a s 6(1) action on a contract outside the SCT Act schedule` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under section 6(1)`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a s 8(6) to (8) action on a relevant contract` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a section 11 regulations action on a time share contract` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under regulations made under section 11`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a section 43(2)(j) action on a relevant contract` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action under provisions specified under section 43(2)(j)`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a motor vehicle deposit action` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `an action relating to a deposit paid in relation to or in contemplation of a motor vehicle sale contract`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an action the Act gives the Tribunal no jurisdiction over` MEANS `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` OF `any other action`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a s 6(1) action on a relevant contract`
#ASSERT NOT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a s 6(1) action on a contract for the sale of immovable property`
#ASSERT NOT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a s 6(1) action on a contract outside the SCT Act schedule`
#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a s 8(6) to (8) action on a relevant contract`
#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a section 11 regulations action on a time share contract`
#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a section 43(2)(j) action on a relevant contract`
#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `a motor vehicle deposit action`
#ASSERT NOT `a Small Claims Tribunal has jurisdiction` `an action the Act gives the Tribunal no jurisdiction over`
#ASSERT `the action is deemed a claim founded on contract for the court limits` `an action under section 6(1)`
#ASSERT NOT `the action is deemed a claim founded on contract for the court limits` `any other action`

-- Relief Facts: court is a Small Claims Tribunal, court finds an unfair practice, action under s 6(1),
-- consumer intends to resell, intends to use up or transform, otherwise business use, share attributed to non-business use.
`a court finds an unfair practice in a consumer's own use` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`a tribunal finds an unfair practice` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`a court finds no unfair practice` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`goods bought to resell, no apportionment` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`goods bought to use up in manufacturing, no apportionment` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING
`services otherwise for business use, apportioned 40 per cent to non-business use` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, JUST 0.4
`business use goods, but the action is not under s 6(1)` MEANS `Relief Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING

#ASSERT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `a court finds an unfair practice in a consumer's own use`
#ASSERT count (`the reliefs the court may grant under section 7(5)` `a court finds an unfair practice in a consumer's own use`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `a tribunal finds an unfair practice`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `a court finds no unfair practice`
#ASSERT null (`the reliefs the court may grant under section 7(5)` `a court finds no unfair practice`)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `goods bought to resell, no apportionment`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `goods bought to use up in manufacturing, no apportionment`
#ASSERT `the goods or services are intended for business use` `goods bought to resell, no apportionment`
#ASSERT `the share of the goods or services for which relief may be granted` `services otherwise for business use, apportioned 40 per cent to non-business use` EQUALS 0.4
#ASSERT `the court may grant relief under section 7(5)` `services otherwise for business use, apportioned 40 per cent to non-business use`
#ASSERT `the share of the goods or services for which relief may be granted` `business use goods, but the action is not under s 6(1)` EQUALS 1

-- Regard Facts: finds an unfair practice occurred, order in an action under s 6(1), scheme available.
#ASSERT `the court must have regard to the consumer's efforts to minimise loss and to resolve the dispute` (`Regard Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court must have regard to the consumer's efforts to minimise loss and to resolve the dispute` (`Regard Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the court must consider whether the consumer sought to resolve the dispute through the specified scheme` (`Regard Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court must consider whether the consumer sought to resolve the dispute through the specified scheme` (`Regard Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `8. Voluntary compliance agreement`

`the not-engage undertaking` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking that the supplier will not engage in the unfair practice`, TRUE, FALSE
`a compensation undertaking the consumer did not ask for` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, TRUE, FALSE
`a compensation undertaking at the consumer's request` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, TRUE, TRUE
`a compensation undertaking the supplier does not agree to` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, FALSE, TRUE
`a reimbursement undertaking` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking to reimburse a specified body for costs or expenses incurred by it`, TRUE, FALSE
`a publicity undertaking` MEANS Undertaking OF `an undertaking to publicise the voluntary compliance agreement`, TRUE, FALSE

-- Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts: body appointed as a specified body, appointment published,
-- reasonable grounds, in writing, the undertakings.
`a written agreement with the not-engage undertaking` MEANS `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, LIST `the not-engage undertaking`, `a publicity undertaking`
`an oral agreement` MEANS `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, LIST `the not-engage undertaking`
`a written agreement without the not-engage undertaking` MEANS `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, LIST `a publicity undertaking`
`a body whose appointment was never gazetted` MEANS `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, LIST `the not-engage undertaking`
`an invitation without reasonable grounds` MEANS `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, LIST `the not-engage undertaking`

#ASSERT `the voluntary compliance agreement satisfies section 8(2)` `a written agreement with the not-engage undertaking`
#ASSERT NOT `the voluntary compliance agreement satisfies section 8(2)` `an oral agreement`
#ASSERT NOT `the voluntary compliance agreement satisfies section 8(2)` `a written agreement without the not-engage undertaking`
#ASSERT `the specified body may invite the supplier to enter into a voluntary compliance agreement` `a written agreement with the not-engage undertaking`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified body may invite the supplier to enter into a voluntary compliance agreement` `a body whose appointment was never gazetted`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified body may invite the supplier to enter into a voluntary compliance agreement` `an invitation without reasonable grounds`
#ASSERT `the undertaking may be included or varied` `a compensation undertaking at the consumer's request`
#ASSERT NOT `the undertaking may be included or varied` `a compensation undertaking the consumer did not ask for`
#ASSERT NOT `the undertaking may be included or varied` `a compensation undertaking the supplier does not agree to`
#ASSERT `the undertaking may be included or varied` `a reimbursement undertaking`
#ASSERT `the undertaking may be included or varied` `a publicity undertaking`

-- Undertaking Enforcement Facts: undertaking enforced, failed to comply, date of failure,
-- date action commenced, recovery already obtained, agreement provides otherwise.
`compensation not paid` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, TRUE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, FALSE, FALSE
`reimbursement not paid` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to reimburse a specified body for costs or expenses incurred by it`, TRUE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, FALSE, FALSE
`publicity not carried out` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to publicise the voluntary compliance agreement`, TRUE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, FALSE, FALSE
`compensation complied with` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, FALSE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, FALSE, FALSE
`compensation already recovered` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, TRUE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, TRUE, FALSE
`compensation already recovered but the agreement provides otherwise` MEANS `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` OF `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`, TRUE, YMD 2025 5 10, YMD 2026 5 10, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the consumer may recover the compensation as a civil debt` `compensation not paid`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified body may recover the reimbursement as a civil debt` `compensation not paid`
#ASSERT `the specified body may recover the reimbursement as a civil debt` `reimbursement not paid`
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may recover the compensation as a civil debt` `reimbursement not paid`
#ASSERT `the specified body may publicise the agreement and recover the costs as a civil debt` `publicity not carried out`
#ASSERT NOT `the consumer may recover the compensation as a civil debt` `compensation complied with`
#ASSERT `recovery bars all further actions to recover the loss, damage, costs or expenses to which the undertaking relates` `compensation already recovered`
#ASSERT NOT `recovery bars all further actions to recover the loss, damage, costs or expenses to which the undertaking relates` `compensation already recovered but the agreement provides otherwise`
#ASSERT NOT `recovery bars all further actions to recover the loss, damage, costs or expenses to which the undertaking relates` `compensation not paid`

§§ `9. Declaration or injunction`

-- Declaration Application Facts: the Commission applies, court, supplier has engaged/is engaging/likely,
-- satisfied it engaged, satisfied it is likely, pending, interim injunction desirable.
`the Commission applies to the District Court, satisfied the supplier engaged` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`the Commission applies to the High Court, satisfied only that it is likely` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF TRUE, `the General Division of the High Court`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`the Commission applies to a Magistrate's Court` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF TRUE, `any other court`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a consumer applies under section 9` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF FALSE, `the District Court`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`the court is satisfied of neither` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`no interim injunction is desirable` MEANS `Declaration Application Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` `the Commission applies to the District Court, satisfied the supplier engaged`
#ASSERT `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` `the Commission applies to the High Court, satisfied only that it is likely`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` `the Commission applies to a Magistrate's Court`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` `a consumer applies under section 9`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a declaration or grant an injunction under section 9(1)` `the court is satisfied of neither`
#ASSERT `the court may grant an interim injunction under section 9(3)` `the Commission applies to the District Court, satisfied the supplier engaged`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant an interim injunction under section 9(3)` `no interim injunction is desirable`
#ASSERT `the court may make accompanying orders under section 9(4)` `the Commission applies to the District Court, satisfied the supplier engaged` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make accompanying orders under section 9(4)` `the Commission applies to the District Court, satisfied the supplier engaged` FALSE

