§§ `10. Injunction against a person knowingly abetting, aiding, permitting or procuring`

-- Abettor Injunction Facts: the Commission applies, court, satisfied the person has abetted,
-- satisfied it is likely, interim desirable, person is an individual, specified period, prescribed in place of 5.
`the Commission applies for an injunction against an abettor` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 5, NOTHING
`the court expects an abettor to abet` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the General Division of the High Court`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 5, NOTHING
`the court is satisfied of neither for an abettor` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 5, NOTHING
`an abettor injunction sought in another court` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `any other court`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 5, NOTHING
`an individual ordered to inform for 6 years` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 6, NOTHING
`an individual ordered to inform for 6 years, the Minister prescribing 7` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 6, JUST 7
`a non-individual with an information order` MEANS `Abettor Injunction Facts` OF TRUE, `the District Court`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, NOTHING

